Hi all

With apologies for self-advertising, there will be two bootcamps this summer:

- 12-16 August 2019: "Corpus Linguistics with R"
- 19-23 August 2019: "Statistics for Linguistics with R"

The former will be based on the relatively new second edition of my corpus linguistics textbook <https://www.amazon.com/dp/1138816280>; the latter will involve chapter 5 of the second edition of my stats book <https://www.amazon.com/dp/3110307286> as prep and then do mixed-effects modeling (with all sorts of add-ons such as a priori and other contrasts, multi-model inferencing, curvature, collinearity, influential data points, imputation ...), classification trees, and random forests. For more organizational information, see here <https://sites.uclouvain.be/bkl-cbl/en/advance-notice-corpus-linguistics-with-r-and-statistics-for-linguistics-with-r-bootcamps-by-s-t-gries/>; for questions about contents, plz ask me.

